%S A399952 0,1,1,2,3,1,4,5,9,4,-5,-1,4,3,7,10,3,13,16,29,45,16,-29,-45,-74,-29,
%T A399952 45,16,61,45,106,61,167,106,273,379,652,1031,379,-652,-273,-925,-652,
%U A399952 -1577,-2229,-3806,-6035,-2229,-8264,-10493,-18757,-29250,-48007,-18757
%N A399952 Deterministic version of the random Fibonacci sequence, with signs from A030190 and the seed as (0,1).
%C A399952 Viswanath's random Fibonacci sequence flips a fair coin for each sign. Reading the signs off one fixed word instead gives a single integer sequence, and A030190 is normal in base 2, so every finite sign pattern still occurs with the frequency a coin would give it. Digit A030190(n-2) drives step n, with "1" adding and "0" subtracting.
%H A399952 Jwalin Bhatt, <a href="/A399952/b399952.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A399952 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/RandomFibonacciSequence.html">Random Fibonacci Sequence</a>
%H A399952 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_Fibonacci_sequence">Random Fibonacci sequence</a>
%F A399952 For n>=2: a(n) = a(n-1) + a(n-2) if A030190(n-2) = 1, otherwise a(n-1) - a(n-2).
%F A399952 Conjecture: lim_{n->oo} |a(n)|^(1/n) = 1.1319882487943... (A078416), Viswanath's constant.
%e A399952 A030190 begins 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0, ..., so the signs applied at steps n = 2, 3, 4, ... are -, +, +, -, +, +, +, -, -, +, ...
%e A399952 a(2) = a(1) - a(0) = 1 - 0 = 1, since A030190(0) = 0.
%e A399952 a(3) = a(2) + a(1) = 1 + 1 = 2, since A030190(1) = 1.
%e A399952 a(4) = a(3) + a(2) = 2 + 1 = 3, since A030190(2) = 1.
%e A399952 a(5) = a(4) - a(3) = 3 - 2 = 1, since A030190(3) = 0.
%o A399952 (Python)
%o A399952 from itertools import count, islice
%o A399952 def A030190():  return (int(d) for m in count(0) for d in bin(m)[2:])
%o A399952 def A399952(n_terms):
%o A399952     a, d = [0, 1], list(islice(A030190(), n_terms))
%o A399952     for n in range(2, n_terms):
%o A399952         a.append(a[n-1] + a[n-2] if d[n-2] else a[n-1] - a[n-2])
%o A399952     return a
%o A399952 print(A399952(54))
%Y A399952 Cf. A000045, A030190, A078416.
%K A399952 sign,new
%O A399952 0,4
